Consider a heterogeneous linearly elastic composite occupying a bounded domain $\Omega \subset \mathbb{R}^3$, whose microstructure is described by $Y$-periodic coefficients with period $\varepsilon > 0$. Let $C^\varepsilon(x) = C(x/\varepsilon)$ denote the (possibly anisotropic) elasticity tensor field, and suppose that, prior to the application of any external load, the composite carries a residual (initial) stress field $\sigma_0^\varepsilon(x) = \sigma_0(x/\varepsilon)$ that is $Y$-periodic, self-equilibrated in the sense that $\operatorname{div}\sigma_0^\varepsilon = 0$ in $\Omega$ with appropriate traction continuity across phase interfaces, but in general nonzero pointwise. Such initial stresses model, for instance, the prestress induced by stretching some constituents (fibers) during manufacture. Under an applied loading inducing a displacement $u^\varepsilon$ and an incremental (deformation-induced) stress $\sigma_d^\varepsilon = C^\varepsilon e(u^\varepsilon)$, the total local stress is $\sigma^\varepsilon = \sigma_0^\varepsilon + \sigma_d^\varepsilon$, and a fracture criterion is typically of the form $F(\sigma^\varepsilon(x)) \le \tau$ or $G(e(u^\varepsilon)(x)) \le \tau$ for prescribed thresholds.

Develop a homogenization theory that, as $\varepsilon \to 0$:

(i) produces an effective constitutive description for the limit displacement and stress fields which correctly incorporates the contribution of the periodic initial stress $\sigma_0$;

(ii) provides a corrector/reconstruction formula expressing the local total stress $\sigma^\varepsilon(x)$ (and local strain) from the macroscopic limit quantities together with the prescribed periodic initial-stress profile $\sigma_0(y)$;

(iii) yields verifiable criteria, in terms of the homogenized solution and the cell-problem correctors, for whether the pointwise local stress or strain reaches the fracture thresholds, taking into account that the initial stresses add to the deformation-induced stresses at the microscale.

Specify the precise function-space framework, the cell problems determining the effective elasticity tensor and the effective initial stress, and prove convergence of $u^\varepsilon$ and of the reconstructed stresses to the homogenized limits.

